  "howItWorksSub": "No internet and no server",
  "howNoInternetTitle": "No internet, no server",
  "howNoInternetBody": "Phones talk to each other directly over Bluetooth or on the same Wi-Fi / hotspot. No account and no phone number.",
  "howMeshTitle": "Mesh network",
  "howMeshBody": "Every phone running Wasl relays for the ones around it, so your message can hop across several phones to reach someone far away.",
  "howEncryptionTitle": "Automatic encryption",
  "howEncryptionBody": "Private chats are end-to-end encrypted with keys made automatically — no password. Phones in the middle only pass messages on and can't read them.",
  "howBothTitle": "Both at once",
  "howBothBody": "Turn on Wi-Fi and Bluetooth together and your phone becomes a bridge: people on one hotspot can reach people on another one through Bluetooth. Calls and video stay inside the same network.",
  "howGroupsTitle": "Groups",
  "howGroupsBody": "Open: anyone nearby can join and read. Password or join request: only members can read. A group stays visible as long as one member is nearby.",
  "howAdminTitle": "Group admins",
  "howAdminBody": "The owner picks admins, and admins can remove members and delete their messages. In a \"join request\" group the key changes when someone is removed, so they can't read new messages; in open and password groups removal is a ban enforced by the apps.",
  "howNotifTitle": "Notifications",
  "howNotifBody": "A notification shows the sender and the message. With the app lock on it only says \"New message\", and the phone's lock screen never shows the text. You can mute any chat.",
  "howSaveTitle": "Saving is optional",
  "howSaveBody": "By default chats aren't saved and are erased when the app closes. If you turn saving on they're stored encrypted, only on your phone.",
  "howSafetyTitle": "Safety code",
  "howSafetyBody": "To be 100% sure you're talking to the right person, compare the safety code (6 digits) from the chat menu. Optional.",
